; FileCheck spec for param_attrs_freeze_lattice.logos — the axes of the Freeze
; lattice plus the unresolved-residue path.
;
; EACH PARAMETER LIST IS PINNED LITERALLY AND EXACTLY, in the same idiom as
; param_attrs_freeze.check: the `{{[^(]*}}` wildcards around the symbol name
; cannot cross a `(`, so they can never absorb an attribute. Every line is
; therefore two-directional — an attribute appearing where it must not, and one
; vanishing where it must be, break the match equally.
;
; ⚠ THE `; AXIS <id>` MARKERS ARE MACHINE-READ. tests/logos/freeze_arm_coverage.py
; derives the VERDICT SITES of `type_is_freeze` from the C++ and requires every
; one of them to name an axis that has a marker here; and every marker here to be
; claimed by a site (or by the EXTRA_AXES section of the ledger). Renaming a
; marker, deleting a CHECK line under one, or adding an arm to the predicate with
; no axis is red by arithmetic, not by anybody remembering to update a list.
;
; LAYOUTS, HAND-DERIVED (all confirmed against the emitted IR afterwards):
;   [Cell<i64>; 4] / [i64; 4]  = 32/8   (Cell<i64> is transparent over
;                                        UnsafeCell<i64> over i64 = 8/8)
;   Outer{Inner{Cell<i64>}, i64} = 16/8
;   PtrField{*mut Cell<i64>}     = 8/8
;   Box2<i64> / Box2<Cell<i64>>  = 8/8
;   Option<i64> / Option<Cell<i64>> = 16/8 (i32 tag padded to the payload's
;                                        align 8, plus the 8-byte payload)
;   (Cell<i64>, i64) / (i64, i64) = 16/8
;   ((Cell<i64>, i64), i64)       = 24/8
;   TupField / TupFieldPlain      = 16/8
;   CLike                         = 4/4  (bare i32 discriminant)
;   SelfCell / SelfPlain          = 16/8 (ptr + 8-byte field)
;   i64                           = 8/8
;   UnsafeCell<i64>               = 8/8
;   AnyVal{raw: i64}              = 8/8  — a USER struct; since task #99
;                                         `is_anyval` demands an empty package,
;                                         so the i32 short-circuit no longer
;                                         steals this declaration's layout

; ── AXIS 1: ARRAY ELEMENT RECURSION ────────────────────────────────────────
; The two pointees have the IDENTICAL 32/8 layout and differ only in the
; element type, so the aliasing pair moving between these two lines can only
; mean the predicate stopped (or started) descending into `[T; N]`.
; AXIS axis_array
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_array_cell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(32) %0)
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_array_plain{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(32) %0)

; ── AXIS 2: DEPTH-2 STRUCT NESTING ─────────────────────────────────────────
; One peel is not a fixpoint. The Cell sits two struct levels down.
; AXIS axis_nested2
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_nested2{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)

; ── AXIS 3: RECURSION STOPS AT AN INDIRECTION ──────────────────────────────
; `*mut Cell<i64>` is a POINTER field: the Cell is not among PtrField's own
; inline bytes, so PtrField IS Freeze and earns the pair. This is rustc parity
; and it is what keeps Rc/Arc — whose refcount lives behind a pointer they LOAD
; — optimizable. If this line ever loses the pair, the exception clause of the
; rule has collapsed and Rc::clone's soundness argument goes with it.
; AXIS axis_ptr_field
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_ptr_field{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── AXIS 4: PER-INSTANCE, NOT PER-DEFINITION ───────────────────────────────
; ONE generic function, two monomorphisations, opposite answers. The concrete
; type argument is a trailing segment of the mangled name (`…Box2$G1$T__i64`
; versus `…Box2$G1$T__Cell$G1$i64`), which is what makes these two lines
; addressable apart. `T__i64` is pinned rather than a bare `i64`, because a bare
; `i64` also occurs inside the Cell mangling and the two patterns would then be
; free to bind to each other's symbol.
;
; ⚠ Note the `{{[^(]*}}` between the name and the `(`: these symbols are
; QUOTE-WRAPPED in the IR (`@"…__i64"(ptr …)`), so the parameter list does not
; follow the name directly. The wildcard still cannot cross a `(`, so it absorbs
; the closing quote and nothing else — the parameter list stays pinned exactly.
; AXIS axis_generic
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_generic{{[^(]*}}Box2{{[^(]*}}T__i64{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_generic{{[^(]*}}Box2{{[^(]*}}T__Cell{{[^(]*}}i64{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── AXIS 5: TWO ENUM INSTANCES COEXISTING ──────────────────────────────────
; Both are `Option`, both 16/8; the answer must be keyed on the instance, not
; cached on the enum name.
; AXIS axis_opt_plain
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_opt_plain{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_opt_cell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_opt_cell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)

; ── AXIS 6: TUPLE ELEMENT RECURSION ────────────────────────────────────────
; THE MEASURED ONE. Replace the element loop with `case K::Tuple: return true;`
; and axis_tuple_cell moves from `ptr noundef align 8` to `ptr noalias noundef
; readonly align 8` — a noalias+readonly on a pointee holding a Cell — while the
; five axes above and L2 (1881/1881) stay green. The control has the IDENTICAL
; 16/8 layout, so nothing but the element type can be blamed.
; AXIS axis_tuple_cell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_tuple_cell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_tuple_plain
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_tuple_plain{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)

; ── AXIS 7: THE TUPLE RECURSION IS A FIXPOINT ──────────────────────────────
; A tuple inside a tuple: 24/8, and the Cell is two tuple levels down.
; AXIS axis_tuple_nested
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_tuple_nested{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(24) %0)

; ── AXIS 8: STRUCT → TUPLE, THE OTHER EDGE ─────────────────────────────────
; Tuple-of-struct is axis 6; this is struct-of-tuple. The struct arm must
; descend into a tuple-typed FIELD, which is a different call edge.
; AXIS axis_tuple_field
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_tuple_field{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_tuple_field_plain
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_tuple_field_plain{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)

; ── AXIS 9: THE C-LIKE ENUM FALLBACK ───────────────────────────────────────
; `resolve_tagged_enum` returns null for a payload-free enum (register_tagged_enum
; runs only under `ed.has_payload()`), and the arm answers `true` on that resolve
; FAILURE — the one non-conservative answer in a predicate whose stated discipline
; is conservative-in-the-safe-direction. The 4/4 here is the load-bearing part: it
; says the pointee really is the bare discriminant scalar the arm assumes, so
; there is no payload for a cell to hide in.
; AXIS axis_clike
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_clike{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 4 dereferenceable(4) %0)

; ── AXIS 10: A SELF-REFERENTIAL STRUCT ─────────────────────────────────────
; Identical 16/8 layouts; only the second field's type moves. Note what this
; does NOT pin: the `seen` cycle branch. A Logos struct cannot contain itself by
; value, so every self-reference goes through an indirection and the indirection
; arm returns before `seen` is consulted. The ledger records that branch as
; UNPINNABLE rather than crediting it to these two lines.
; AXIS axis_selfref_cell
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_selfref_cell{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)
; AXIS axis_selfref_plain
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_selfref_plain{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(16) %0)

; ── AXIS 11: A BARE SCALAR POINTEE ─────────────────────────────────────────
; The scalar arm is the control for every other axis and was pinned by nothing
; of its own.
; AXIS axis_scalar
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_scalar{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── AXIS 12: THE UnsafeCell LANG ITEM, DIRECTLY ────────────────────────────
; Every other axis reaches this arm by field recursion. Here the pointee IS the
; lang item, so the pkg-qualified-name arm is what answers. If that arm ever
; loses its `pkg_name() == "logos.lang.cell"` guard — or gains a wrong one — this
; line moves and nothing else in the file does.
; AXIS axis_unsafecell_item
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_unsafecell_item{{[^(]*}}(ptr noundef align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── AXIS 13: THE `is_anyval` SHORT-CIRCUIT DOES NOT FIRE FOR A USER STRUCT ──
; RE-AIMED 2026-08-22 (task #99). This line used to pin `align 4
; dereferenceable(4)`, and the comment above it said so approvingly: `is_anyval`
; matched any struct NAMED AnyVal in ANY package and lowered it as an i32. But
; `AnyVal` in THIS file is a LOCAL user declaration — `struct AnyVal { raw: i64 }`
; at line 145, the only `struct AnyVal` in the whole tree — so the 4/4 the check
; pinned was the compiler assigning the user's 8-byte struct the compiler's own
; internal 4-byte representation. The same short-circuit made `u.raw` read back
; as garbage (`raw=-8757281498698088448`, varying run to run, exit 1 instead of
; 20, NO diagnostic). The pin asserted the DEFECT as expected output.
;
; `is_anyval` is now FQN-checked like `is_stdlib_box`: it demands an EMPTY
; package, which is what the compiler's own synthesised AnyVal carries and what
; a user declaration never does. So this axis now pins the CORRECT lowering —
; `{ raw: i64 }` is 8/8 by the ordinary Struct route — and it is the NEGATIVE
; pin for the shadowing hazard: if the qualification is ever dropped, the
; short-circuit fires again and this line goes back to 4/4 and red.
; ⚠ It still pins the ANSWER, not the arm's existence: the Struct arm answers
; Freeze for `{ raw: i64 }` too, so the `noalias readonly` pair is unmoved.
; The arm's OWN reachability is not observable from this file at all any more —
; only the compiler-synthesised, un-packaged AnyVal reaches it, and no source
; program declares one. Stated in the ledger, not implied.
; AXIS axis_anyval
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}axis_anyval{{[^(]*}}(ptr noalias noundef readonly align 8 dereferenceable(8) %0)

; ── RESIDUE: CONSERVATIVE ON AN UNRESOLVABLE POINTEE ────────────────────────
; `Id::call`'s second parameter is the HRTB binder's `&'a T` — a bare TypeVar,
; no instance of which exists. `align`/`dereferenceable` are a LAYOUT CLAIM and
; must be OMITTED rather than guessed (a declined `layout_of` used to return
; `{8,8}`, and that guess was written into the object file). `noalias`/
; `readonly` are absent too, because nothing is known about the pointee — this
; is the `default:` arm of the predicate, the conservative-on-unknown one.
;
; ⚠ THIS LINE IS THE STRICTEST IN THE FILE AND MUST STAY THAT WAY. It pins the
; WHOLE parameter list including the leading by-value `self`, so an `align` or
; `dereferenceable` reappearing on a residue param — the exact regression that
; wrote a guessed alignment into an object file — cannot hide behind a wildcard.
; AXIS axis_residue
; CHECK-DAG: define {{.*}}@{{[^(]*}}Id__call{{[^(]*}}(ptr %0, ptr noundef %1)
